></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA TATSUNORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MORIMOTO TAKAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO MASAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUJIWARA, TATSUNORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORIMOTO, TAKAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, MASAO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A CD (disc) is carried in by a CD carrying mechanism including a carrying roller (11) for mounting on a turntable.  An MD (cartridge-built-in disc) (24) is carried in by an MD carrying mechanism, while being fitted in a holder (25), for mounting on the turntable.  A carrying roller moving mechanism is provided which moves the carrying roller (11) to a position below the position at which the CD is inserted and toward a disc insertion side away from an optical pickup for the CD as the CD carried in by the CD carrying mechanism is mounted on the turntable and which returns the carrying roller (11), moved to below the position and toward the insertion side, to the position at the insertion time when the CD is removed from the surface of the turntable.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Un disque compact (CD) est supporté dans et par un mécanisme de support de CD comprenant un galet (11) de support destiné à être monté sur une platine. Un disque cartouche (24) est supporté dans et par un mécanisme de disque cartouche alors qu'il est introduit dans un support (25), en vue d'être monté sur la platine. Un mécanisme de déplacement du galet de support est prévu, ce dernier déplace le galet (11) de support jusqu'à une position où il se trouve en dessous de la position à laquelle le CD est introduit et orienté vers un côté d'introduction du disque loin d'un lecteur optique de CD lorsque ce dernier, supporté par le mécanisme de support de CD est monté sur la platine, et renvoie le galet (11) de support, déplacé jusqu'à une position inférieure à la position du côté introduction, en direction de ce dernier, jusqu'à la position au moment de l'introduction où le CD est enlevé de la surface de la platine.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>